<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-ZA">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
<title>Shape Dash</title>
<style>
:root{
  --purple:#6c4ce0; --purple-d:#54389f; --teal:#12b5a5; --teal-d:#0d8c80;
  --bg:#f4f2fc; --card:#ffffff; --ink:#2b2350; --sub:#6f6a8a;
  --good:#1fa552; --bad:#e0485a; --warn:#f2a51a; --line:#e6e2f5;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box; -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent;}
html,body{margin:0;padding:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
  font-family:-apple-system,'SF Pro Rounded',BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;
  height:100%; overscroll-behavior:none;}
#app{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:14px 16px 40px;min-height:100%;}
.topbar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:6px 2px 12px;}
.brand{font-weight:800;font-size:20px;color:var(--purple);letter-spacing:.3px;}
.brand span{color:var(--teal);}
.streak{font-weight:700;color:var(--warn);font-size:16px;}
.pbar{height:12px;background:#e4dff7;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;margin:2px 0 16px;}
.pbar>div{height:100%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--teal),var(--purple));border-radius:8px;transition:width .4s;}
.card{background:var(--card);border-radius:20px;padding:20px;box-shadow:0 3px 14px rgba(80,60,160,.08);margin-bottom:16px;}
.study{border:2px solid var(--purple);border-radius:16px;padding:14px 16px;background:#faf9ff;margin:12px 0;}
.study h4{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--purple);font-size:15px;}
h1{font-size:26px;margin:8px 0 6px;} h2{font-size:21px;margin:4px 0 10px;}
p{line-height:1.5;} .sub{color:var(--sub);font-size:15px;}
.big{font-size:22px;line-height:1.6;}
.qtext{font-size:22px;line-height:1.7;margin:6px 0 14px;}
.qtext u{text-decoration-color:var(--teal);text-decoration-thickness:3px;}
.frac{display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;vertical-align:middle;margin:0 3px;font-size:.8em;line-height:1.15;}
.frac>span:first-child{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);padding:0 4px;}
.frac>span:last-child{padding:0 4px;}
.btn{display:block;width:100%;border:none;border-radius:16px;padding:16px;font-size:19px;font-weight:700;
  font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer;margin-top:12px;min-height:58px;}
.btn:active{transform:scale(.985);}
.btn-main{background:var(--purple);color:#fff;}
.btn-teal{background:var(--teal);color:#fff;}
.btn-soft{background:#ece8fb;color:var(--purple-d);}
.btn-ghost{background:none;color:var(--sub);font-weight:600;font-size:16px;min-height:44px;padding:10px;}
.btn:disabled{opacity:.45;}
.choices{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;margin:10px 0;}
.choices.row{flex-direction:row;} .choices.row .choice{flex:1;text-align:center;font-size:26px;}
.choice{border:2px solid var(--line);background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:14px 16px;font-size:20px;
  font-weight:600;font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink);}
.choice.sel{border-color:var(--purple);background:#f1edff;}
.answer-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin:8px 0;}
.answer-row label{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;}
input.ans{flex:1;border:2px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:14px;font-size:24px;font-family:inherit;
  min-width:120px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink);}
input.ans:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--teal);}
.canvas-wrap{border:2px dashed #cfc8ee;border-radius:16px;background:#fff;position:relative;margin:12px 0 4px;}
.canvas-label{position:absolute;top:8px;left:12px;color:#b9b2d8;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;pointer-events:none;}
canvas.work{width:100%;height:240px;border-radius:14px;touch-action:none;display:block;}
.tools{display:flex;gap:8px;margin:6px 0 2px;}
.tool{flex:0 0 auto;border:2px solid var(--line);background:#fff;border-radius:12px;padding:8px 14px;
  font-size:15px;font-weight:700;font-family:inherit;color:var(--sub);cursor:pointer;}
.tool.on{border-color:var(--teal);color:var(--teal-d);background:#eafaf8;}
.feedback{border-radius:16px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:12px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;}
.fb-good{background:#e6f7ec;border:2px solid var(--good);}
.fb-bad{background:#fdeef0;border:2px solid var(--bad);}
.fb-hint{background:#fff8e8;border:2px solid var(--warn);}
.sol{background:#f1edff;border:2px solid var(--purple);border-radius:16px;padding:14px 16px;margin-top:12px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;}
.mastery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin:14px 0;}
.skill-tile{background:#fff;border-radius:14px;padding:12px;border:2px solid var(--line);}
.skill-tile b{font-size:14px;display:block;margin-bottom:6px;}
.meter{height:10px;background:#eee9fb;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;}
.meter>div{height:100%;border-radius:6px;transition:width .5s;}
.badges{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:10px 0;}
.badge{background:#fff;border:2px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;}
.badge.won{border-color:var(--warn);background:#fff8e8;}
.center{text-align:center;}
.emoji-big{font-size:56px;margin:10px 0;}
.timer{font-size:30px;font-weight:800;color:var(--purple);text-align:center;letter-spacing:1px;}
.timer.low{color:var(--bad);}
table.dash{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px;}
table.dash th,table.dash td{padding:8px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}
.pill{display:inline-block;border-radius:10px;padding:2px 10px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;}
.pill.g{background:var(--good);} .pill.b{background:var(--bad);} .pill.w{background:var(--warn);}
img.hw{max-width:100%;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:#fff;}
textarea.note{width:100%;border:2px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:10px;font-family:inherit;font-size:16px;min-height:60px;}
.small{font-size:14px;color:var(--sub);}
.rowflex{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;}
svg.nline{width:100%;height:auto;margin:8px 0;}
.hidden{display:none;}
a.linkbtn{display:block;text-align:center;text-decoration:none;}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="app"></div>
<script>
"use strict";
/* ============ utilities ============ */
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
const app=document.getElementById('app');
const ri=(a,b)=>a+Math.floor(Math.random()*(b-a+1));
const pick=a=>a[Math.floor(Math.random()*a.length)];
const shuffle=a=>{a=a.slice();for(let i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1));[a[i],a[j]]=[a[j],a[i]];}return a;};
const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/&/g,'&amp;').replace(/</g,'&lt;').replace(/>/g,'&gt;').replace(/"/g,'&quot;');
/* decimals as scaled integers: fmt(v,dp) -> SA comma string. fmt(1234,2)="12,34" */
function fmt(v,dp){ if(dp===0) return String(v);
  let s=String(Math.abs(v)).padStart(dp+1,'0');
  let w=s.slice(0,-dp), f=s.slice(-dp);
  return (v<0?'−':'')+w+','+f; }
function trimz(str){ /* remove unnecessary zeros from "5,080" -> "5,08" */
  if(!str.includes(',')) return str;
  let [w,f]=str.split(','); f=f.replace(/0+$/,'');
  return f.length? w+','+f : w; }
function parseNum(s){ if(s==null)return null; s=String(s).trim().replace(/\s+/g,'').replace(',','.').replace('−','-');
  if(!/^-?(\d+\.?\d*|\.\d+)$/.test(s)) return null; return parseFloat(s); }
function numEq(a,b){ return Math.abs(a-b)<1e-9; }
function fr(n,d){ return '<span class="frac"><span>'+n+'</span><span>'+d+'</span></span>'; }
/* ============ skills (Paper 2) ============ */
const SKILLS={
 s1:{name:'2-D Shapes & Quadrilaterals',emoji:'🔷',color:'#6c4ce0',essential:true},
 s2:{name:'Angles',emoji:'📐',color:'#12b5a5',essential:true},
 s3:{name:'3-D Objects',emoji:'🧊',color:'#f97316',essential:true},
 s4:{name:'Symmetry & Views',emoji:'🪞',color:'#3b82f6',essential:false},
 s5:{name:'Geometric Patterns',emoji:'🔁',color:'#8b5cf6',essential:false},
 s6:{name:'Capacity (mℓ, ℓ, kℓ)',emoji:'🥤',color:'#10b981',essential:true},
 s7:{name:'Mass (g, kg, t)',emoji:'⚖️',color:'#e0485a',essential:true},
 s8:{name:'Data Handling & Graphs',emoji:'📊',color:'#f2a51a',essential:true}
};
const LESSONS={
 s1:{title:'2-D Shapes & Quadrilaterals',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>A <b>polygon</b> is a flat 2-D shape with only <b>straight</b> sides, and it must be <b>closed</b>. Polygons are named by their number of sides: triangle 3, quadrilateral 4, pentagon 5, hexagon 6, heptagon 7, octagon 8, <b>nona</b>gon 9, <b>deca</b>gon 10.</p>
   <p>A <b>regular</b> polygon has ALL sides equal <i>and</i> all angles equal. Otherwise it is <b>irregular</b>.</p>
   <p>Special quadrilaterals: a <b>square</b> (4 equal sides, 4 right angles), a <b>rectangle</b> (2 pairs of equal sides, 4 right angles), a <b>parallelogram</b> (2 pairs of parallel sides), a <b>rhombus</b> (4 equal sides, no right angles needed), a <b>trapezium</b> (exactly <b>one</b> pair of parallel sides) and a <b>kite</b> (2 pairs of neighbouring equal sides, <b>no</b> parallel sides).</p>
   <p><b>Parallel lines</b> stay the same distance apart and never meet … but they do NOT have to be the same length!</p></div>`},
 s2:{title:'Angles',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>From smallest to biggest:</p>
   <p><b>Acute</b> … smaller than a right angle (less than 90°)<br>
   <b>Right</b> … a perfect corner (90°)<br>
   <b>Obtuse</b> … bigger than a right angle but smaller than a straight angle<br>
   <b>Straight</b> … a straight line (180°) = 2 right angles<br>
   <b>Reflex</b> … bigger than a straight angle but smaller than a revolution<br>
   <b>Revolution</b> … a full turn (360°) = 4 right angles</p>
   <p>Clock trick: at <b>3 o'clock</b> the hands make a <b>right</b> angle, at <b>6 o'clock</b> a <b>straight</b> angle.</p></div>`},
 s3:{title:'3-D Objects',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>A <b>face</b> is a flat surface. An <b>edge</b> is where two faces meet. A <b>vertex</b> is the point where edges meet.</p>
   <p>A <b>cube</b>: 6 faces, 12 edges, 8 vertices. A <b>rectangular prism</b>: also 6, 12, 8.<br>
   A <b>triangular prism</b>: 5 faces, 9 edges, 6 vertices.<br>
   A <b>square-based pyramid</b>: 5 faces, 8 edges, 5 vertices.<br>
   A <b>triangular pyramid</b> (tetrahedron): 4 faces, 6 edges, 4 vertices.</p>
   <p><b>Prisms</b> have two identical <b>end</b> faces. <b>Pyramids</b> have one base and meet at a point. A <b>cylinder</b>, <b>cone</b> and <b>sphere</b> have <b>curved</b> surfaces … so they are neither prisms nor pyramids. The base of a cone is a <b>circle</b>.</p></div>`},
 s4:{title:'Symmetry & Views',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>A <b>line of symmetry</b> divides a shape in half so that one side fits <b>exactly</b> on the other when folded.</p>
   <p>A <b>square</b> has 4 lines of symmetry, a <b>rectangle</b> only 2 … its diagonal is NOT a line of symmetry! A <b>parallelogram</b> has <b>0</b> … surprising but true. Letters: A has 1, H has 2, Z has 0.</p>
   <p><b>Views:</b> the <b>front view</b> of a cube stack is what you see standing in front (columns as tall as the stacks). The <b>top view</b> is looking straight down. Count hidden cubes too!</p></div>`},
 s5:{title:'Geometric Patterns',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>A <b>constant difference</b> means the same number of shapes is added for each new figure.</p>
   <p>Work out the difference between Figure 1 and Figure 2 … that is your jump. The <b>rule</b> connects the figure number to the count, for example: number of matches = figure number × 2 + 1.</p>
   <p>To find Figure 15, do NOT draw 15 figures … use the rule!</p></div>`},
 s6:{title:'Capacity: mℓ, ℓ and kℓ',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>mℓ → ℓ: <b>divide by 1000</b>. &nbsp; ℓ → mℓ: <b>multiply by 1000</b>. &nbsp; ℓ → kℓ: divide by 1000 again.</p>
   <p class="big">5000 mℓ = 5 ℓ &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2578 mℓ = 2,578 ℓ &nbsp;·&nbsp; 400 mℓ = 0,4 ℓ</p>
   <p>Watch the zeros: 2050 mℓ = 2,05 ℓ … NOT 2,5 ℓ! And no unnecessary end zeros: 2500 mℓ = 2,5 ℓ.</p>
   <p>When adding or subtracting, first make the units the <b>same</b>: 1,5 ℓ + 435 mℓ = 1500 mℓ + 435 mℓ = 1935 mℓ.</p></div>`},
 s7:{title:'Mass: g, kg and tons',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>g → kg: <b>divide by 1000</b>. &nbsp; kg → g: <b>multiply by 1000</b>. &nbsp; kg → t: divide by 1000 (1 ton = 1000 kg).</p>
   <p class="big">3000 g = 3 kg &nbsp;·&nbsp; 5479 g = 5,479 kg &nbsp;·&nbsp; 80 g = 0,08 kg</p>
   <p><b>Price per kilogram</b>: R45 for 3 kg means R45 ÷ 3 = <b>R15 per 1 kg</b>. For grams, think in fractions of a kg: 500 g is half, so half the price.</p>
   <p>Adding: make units the same first! 1,73 kg + 826 g = 1730 g + 826 g = 2556 g = 2,556 kg.</p></div>`},
 s8:{title:'Data Handling & Graphs',html:
  `<div class="study"><h4>📖 Study</h4>
   <p>The <b>mode</b> is the number that appears <b>most</b> (m<b>o</b>de … m<b>o</b>st). The <b>median</b> is the <b>middle</b> number … but FIRST write the numbers in order from lowest to highest! If two numbers share the middle, the median is halfway between them.</p>
   <p><b>Tally marks</b> count in groups of 5 (four strokes and a line through). The count is called the <b>frequency</b>.</p>
   <p>In a <b>pictograph</b>, check the KEY: if ⬤ = 8 learners, then 2½ symbols = 20 learners.</p>
   <p>In <b>bar graphs</b>, read the height of each bar off the scale. In <b>pie charts</b>, the fractions of the circle share the total: ¼ of 96 = 24.</p></div>`}
};
